<title>TURKEY: Turkish Eximbank secures $100-mln syndicated loan.</title>
<headline>Turkish Eximbank secures $100-mln syndicated loan.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkey's Export-Import Bank has secured a $100 million syndicated loan, the bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>It said the one-year loan was given by a 19-bank consortium including ABN Amro, Citibank, Credit Lyonnais, The Sakura Bank, The Sanwa Bank, Societe Generale and West LB.</p>
<p>The loan carries an interest rate of LIBOR plus 75 basis points.</p>
<p>The acccord for the loan, initially planned for $75 million, will be signed on Friday.</p>
</text>
